{"code":200,"message":"OK","tweet":{"url":"https://x.com/OcanaSantero/status/2115442970530857372","id":"2115442970530857372","text":"EARLY conclusions \n\nAutonomous surgical robots exist and they are better at the mechanics than our bench rig tbh. But in every one of them, a human decided what operation to perform, and the robot executed it.\n\nNobody told this agent what to give or where to put it. It got a phenotype and a shelf of candidates and had to work out the therapy and the coordinates itself. I am not aware of an agent previously choosing a treatment and a brain target and then delivering it into a living mammal.\n\nThis is what we mean by in vivo lab in the loop. FULLY connecting agents to our experimental capabilities. More on this soon. \n\nP.S.: Mouse recovered well!\n\nFull write-up soon on substack","raw_text":{"text":"EARLY conclusions \n\nAutonomous surgical robots exist and they are better at the mechanics than our bench rig tbh. But in every one of them, a human decided what operation to perform, and the robot executed it.\n\nNobody told this agent what to give or where to put it. It got a phenotype and a shelf of candidates and had to work out the therapy and the coordinates itself. I am not aware of an agent previously choosing a treatment and a brain target and then delivering it into a living mammal.\n\nThis is what we mean by in vivo lab in the loop. FULLY connecting agents to our experimental capabilities. More on this soon. \n\nP.S.: Mouse recovered well!\n\nFull write-up soon on substack","display_text_range":[0,683],"facets":[{"type":"media","indices":[276,299],"id":"2115380549229613056","display":"pic.x.com/WIuISlCt4Q","original":"https://t.co/WIuISlCt4Q","replacement":"https://x.com/OcanaSantero/status/2115442970530857372/video/1"}]},"author":{"screen_name":"OcanaSantero","url":"https://x.com/OcanaSantero","id":"1480939368437235721","followers":3356,"following":207,"likes":319,"media_count":45,"name":"Gabriel Ocana-Santero","descripti